{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779133949,"nonce":"WQJStEb2AG1dmAsTTHnoqlXenWE=","title":"Studio Scenario Workspace Slice 3: objective authoring and canonical objective terms","message":"## Parent\n\nChild of `5378a5d`, comment `503c7f8`. Depends on Slices 1 and 2.\n\n## Purpose\n\nMake the first integrated scenario-authoring workflow: objectives become first-class editable relationship objects, with current executable loss specs as lowering targets rather than the primary UI model.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Promote authoring around `StudioObjectiveTermSpec` or the local equivalent.\n- Add graph entry points such as `Add objective from here` for graph ports/state/probes/edges where practical.\n- Add Workspace source-target objective creation for initial effector-to-goal or effector-to-trajectory cases when the scenario has enough information.\n- Add objective badges/overlays or relationship indicators on referenced graph/workspace entities.\n- Add objective edit/delete/disable support in Objectives projection and inspector.\n- Lower edited objective terms to the current training loss/metric execution structures at validation or launch time.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A user-created objective appears in Objectives, marks relevant graph/workspace entities, persists in scenario state, validates, and lowers to executable training loss state.\n- Existing legacy loss terms still appear as imported/lowered objective terms without pretending they were authored through the new UI.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Add unit tests for objective creation, update, deletion/disable, selector handling, and lowering.\n- Run focused frontend tests.\n- Run relevant backend or Python tests if lowering touches backend code.\n- Run `npm run build` from `web`.\n\n## Branch\n\nSuggested feature branch: `feature/studio-scenario-slice3-objectives`.","files":null}]}